## Context

Step D of 0978. Run the whole cutover end to end in a disposable HOME seeded with a copy of
the repository, before touching the live one. Extends the 2026-09-28 rollback prototype
(23 crash points) from fixture to full shape.

Traps the rehearsal must cover: every worktree's `.git` file holds an absolute
`gitdir: $HOME/.claude/.git/worktrees/...` (needs `git worktree repair`); the
cwd-keyed project memory and `~/.claude.json` entries (0984's remedy); the per-entry links
one level down in `projects/*/memory`; the systemd timers, especially `claude-refresh`
which pulls `~/.claude` daily.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] One script performs the cutover and one the rollback; both idempotent, both refuse on a dirty tree or a foreign file
- [ ] In the disposable HOME: after cutover, the 0983 validator passes and a fresh session loads hooks, skills, CLAUDE.md and memory (0984 sentinel); after rollback, bytes and link targets match the pre-state
- [ ] Worktrees survive (repair tested), timers are paused and resumed by the script
- [ ] A checklist for the live window is written, including the quiet-window preconditions

Carried over from 0983 (PR #1055 review):

- [ ] The rehearsal rewrites the projection manifest (`adapters/projections.json`) for the post-cutover layout and runs the validator before the first launch; the unrewritten manifest must be shown to refuse (it encodes `~/.claude` as the checkout)
